[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255124462","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737#issuecomment-1255124462","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737","id":1255124462,"node_id":"IC_kwDOANpJv85Kz63u","user":{"login":"ericniebler","id":225757,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTc1Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-22T14:38:53Z","updated_at":"2022-09-22T14:38:53Z","body":"I don't think this is a bug. The elements must be partially ordered, IIRC. The presence of inf in the range violates the algorithm's preconditions.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255124462/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255152193","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737#issuecomment-1255152193","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737","id":1255152193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOANpJv85K0BpB","user":{"login":"mathysie","id":26286382,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2Mjg2Mzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26286382?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie","html_url":"https://github.com/mathysie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-22T14:58:50Z","updated_at":"2022-09-22T14:58:50Z","body":"Thank you for the quick response!\r\n\r\nIf I check the docs (https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/algorithm/nth_element), there is no mention of a precondition apart from having two random access iterators pointing to the first en last elements of the range. Furthermore, according to (https://www.gnu.org/software/libc/manual/html_node/Infinity-and-NaN.html) we have `(infinity < infinity) == false`. Therefore I do not expect issues when sorting ranges containing infinities as infinity is not defined as smaller than infinity.\r\n\r\nI'll check whether the MSVC-compiler defers from this and applies `(infinity < infinity) == true`.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255152193/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255375213","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737#issuecomment-1255375213","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737","id":1255375213,"node_id":"IC_kwDOANpJv85K04Ft","user":{"login":"ericniebler","id":225757,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTc1Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-22T18:06:52Z","updated_at":"2022-09-22T18:06:52Z","body":"For `a` and `b` to be partially ordered relative to each other, at most one of these must be true:\r\n\r\n`a < b`\r\n`b < a`\r\n\r\nThat's not true for infinity.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255375213/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255386931","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737#issuecomment-1255386931","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737","id":1255386931,"node_id":"IC_kwDOANpJv85K068z","user":{"login":"ericniebler","id":225757,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTc1Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericniebler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-22T18:18:58Z","updated_at":"2022-09-22T18:18:58Z","body":":facepalm: I'm thinking of NaN.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255386931/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255936891","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737#issuecomment-1255936891","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737","id":1255936891,"node_id":"IC_kwDOANpJv85K3BN7","user":{"login":"mathysie","id":26286382,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2Mjg2Mzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26286382?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie","html_url":"https://github.com/mathysie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-23T08:33:07Z","updated_at":"2022-09-23T08:36:27Z","body":"Yes, we initially made this mistake as well. We previously used `NaN` and got good results due to the used compiler, as the real behaviour of comparison with `NaN` and `double` is undefined. To make the results compiler-independent we refactored `NaN` to `infinity` to have all defined comparisons and pushed the code to production with the ranges v3-library of date 2021-11-02. \r\n\r\nAfter updating to version 0.12, the given input started to crash.\r\n\r\nI tested the comparisons with `infinity`, which gave the following output:\r\n```cpp\r\ndouble a = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();\r\ndouble b = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();\r\n\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a < b) << std::endl;  // false\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a > b) << std::endl;  // false\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a == b) << std::endl; // true\r\n```\r\nFurthermore, comparison `infinity` with a 'standard' double gives:\r\n```cpp\r\ndouble a = 42.37;\r\ndouble b = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();\r\n\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a < b) << std::endl;  // true\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a > b) << std::endl;  // false\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a == b) << std::endl; // false\r\n```\r\nThis seems to me like `infinity` having a well-defined partial ordering in our input vector.\r\n\r\nWhereas NaN does indeed not have a well-defined partial ordering with our compiler:\r\n```cpp\r\ndouble a = std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN();\r\ndouble b = std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN();\r\n\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a < b) << std::endl;  // false\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a > b) << std::endl;  // false\r\nstd::cout << std::boolalpha << (a == b) << std::endl; // false\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1255936891/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1256119673","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737#issuecomment-1256119673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1737","id":1256119673,"node_id":"IC_kwDOANpJv85K3t15","user":{"login":"mathysie","id":26286382,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2Mjg2Mzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26286382?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie","html_url":"https://github.com/mathysie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathysie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-23T11:57:47Z","updated_at":"2022-09-23T11:57:47Z","body":"So in my opinion the algorithm should support `infinity` along with `double`'s","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/1256119673/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]